    "result_text": "The build is green. The full suite (which contains the one acceptance test) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the city-capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when the target city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the existing household-conflict pattern in this OfficeFloor pipeline, I added:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners in the request's city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed match, consistent with `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`) and throws when the count is \u2265 50. It runs after validation and before `BuildOwner`, so an at-capacity city returns 409 rather than persisting a record.\n- **`OwnerCityAtCapacityException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) \u2014 carries the city and count.\n- **`OwnerCityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `409 Conflict` via `ObjectResponse`.\n- **Escalation YAML** `officefloor/escalation/\u2026OwnerCityAtCapacityException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n- Wired a `checkCityCapacity` step into `owners.POST.yml` (after `checkHousehold`, before `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`).\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
